    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always had a mixed relationship with mathematics. While I studied it through my master’s degree, I find it less engaging than philosophy or art. My parents—especially my father with his PhD—taught me the basics, but I never developed a deep passion. I see math as a tool, not a subject of true interest. I enjoy its logic, but it doesn’t spark the same curiosity as creative or human-centered fields.",
